# PROJECT: DISASTERGUARD AI
## Complete Full-Stack Disaster Monitoring, Intelligence, Historical Research and Early-Warning Platform

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, UI/UX designer, AI/ML engineer, IoT systems engineer, GIS developer, database architect and cybersecurity specialist.

Your task is to design and build a complete, professional, production-oriented web application named **DisasterGuard AI**.

This is not a simple dashboard, landing page, static website, or UI-only prototype.

Build a connected disaster-monitoring and intelligence platform designed to work with a physical solar-powered, multi-hazard monitoring pole containing environmental sensors, a microcontroller, communication modules, a solar power system, an emergency beacon and controlled alert equipment.

The platform should be suitable for a serious national-level school science exhibition and research project, with a professional appearance comparable to a modern government disaster-management command and intelligence platform.

The application must have:
- A fully developed frontend.
- A functional backend.
- A structured database.
- Secure authentication and role-based access.
- Live IoT sensor integration architecture.
- AI-powered hazard analysis.
- Historical disaster records covering approximately the last ten years.
- Interactive GIS maps.
- Pole and sensor management.
- Alert management.
- An advanced simulation and demonstration laboratory.
- A separate demonstration-data environment.
- Professional reports and analytics.

Do not stop after generating a homepage or dashboard mockup. Build the complete application, including working navigation, functional buttons, database operations, forms, charts, filters, maps, and realistic data flows.

