The system must explicitly explain that:

A P-wave is generally the first seismic wave to arrive. Earthquake early-warning systems detect an earthquake after it begins and may provide a limited warning to locations farther from the source before stronger shaking arrives.

A single low-cost accelerometer on a pole cannot provide a validated P-wave earthquake early-warning system.

Never label a vibration anomaly as a confirmed earthquake without appropriate validation.

Never claim to predict earthquake location, magnitude or occurrence time.

